`clearToolCall()` removes the callID from the per-session Set/Map but never removes the (now possibly empty) Set/Map entries for that session. Over time, an agent handling many short-lived sessions/tool calls may retain lots of empty collections. Consider deleting `toolStarts[sessionID]` / `bashSnapshots[sessionID]` when their size drops to 0 (or consolidating cleanup into `clearToolCall`).
```suggestion
    const toolStarts = this.toolStarts.get(sessionID)
    toolStarts?.delete(callID)
    if (toolStarts?.size === 0) {
      this.toolStarts.delete(sessionID)
    }

    const bashSnapshots = this.bashSnapshots.get(sessionID)
    bashSnapshots?.delete(callID)
    if (bashSnapshots?.size === 0) {
      this.bashSnapshots.delete(sessionID)
    }
```

